# Force LF line endings for every text file, regardless of a given
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Found while reconciling the
# Pi's own on-disk deploy state against origin/main: several files had
# picked up CRLF at some point (from being scp'd from a Windows checkout),
# which is harmless to Python/Bash on Linux but produces a 100%-of-lines
# "diff" against the git-stored LF blob, making real content drift
# impossible to spot at a glance. This guarantees every checkout - on any
# OS, any contributor - normalizes to LF, so a future sync's diff only ever
# shows genuine content changes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files - never text-normalize these.
*.JPG binary
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
